WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.030
During this past year, I’ve had three instances of car trouble.
过去这一年里，我的车出过三次毛病。

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:10.750
Each time these things happened, I was sick of the way most people hadn’t bothered to help.
每次出这种事，大多数人都懒得帮忙，这让我很是厌烦。

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:16.670
One of those times, I was on the side of the road for close to three hours with my big Jeep.
其中有一次，我开着那辆大吉普车，在路边困了将近三个小时。

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:22.300
I put signs in the windows, big signs that said NEED A JACK, and offered money.
我在车窗上贴了牌子，大大的牌子上写着“需要千斤顶”，还说愿意出钱。

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:23.760
Nothing.
毫无回应。

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:30.800
Right as I was about to give up, a Mexican family in a small truck pulled over, and the father bounded out.
就在我快要放弃的时候，一个墨西哥家庭开着一辆小卡车靠边停下，那位父亲一跃跳下车来。

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.760
He sized up the situation and called for his daughter, who spoke English.
他打量了一下情况，把会说英语的女儿叫了过来。

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:42.830
He conveyed through her that he had a jack but that it was too small for the Jeep, so we would need something to support it.
他通过女儿告诉我，他有一个千斤顶，可对吉普车来说太小了，所以我们得找个东西把它垫高。

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:48.320
Then he got a saw from the truck and cut a section out of a big log on the side of the road.
接着，他从卡车上拿了一把锯子，从路边一根大圆木上锯下一截。

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.860
We rolled it over and put his jack on top, and we were in business.
我们把木头滚过来，把他的千斤顶放在上面，这下就能干活了。

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:59.410
I started taking the wheel off, and then, if you can believe it, I broke his tire iron.
我开始拆轮子，接着，说出来你都不信，我把他的轮胎扳手弄断了。

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:06.630
No worries: He handed it to his wife, and she was gone in a flash down the road to buy a new tire iron.
没关系：他把扳手递给妻子，她一眨眼就沿着路开走了，去买一把新的轮胎扳手。

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:09.070
She was back in 15 minutes.
十五分钟后她就回来了。

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:12.750
We finished the job, and I was a very happy man.
我们干完了活，我开心极了。

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:15.390
The two of us were dirty and sweaty.
我们俩又脏又满身是汗。

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:19.390
His wife prepared a pot of water for us to wash our hands.
他妻子准备了一盆水，让我们洗手。

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:28.870
I tried to put a $20 bill in the man’s hand, but he wouldn’t take it, so instead I went up to the truck and gave it to his wife as quietly as I could.
我想把一张二十美元的钞票塞到那人手里，可他不肯收，于是我转而走到卡车那边，尽量不声不响地把钱给了他妻子。

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:31.510
I asked the little girl where they lived.
我问小女孩他们住在哪儿。

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:33.450
Mexico, she said.
墨西哥，她说。

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:39.060
They were in Oregon so Mommy and Daddy could work on a fruit farm for the next few weeks.
他们来俄勒冈，是为了让爸爸妈妈接下来几个星期在一家水果农场干活。

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.040
Then they would go home.
然后他们就要回家了。

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.440
When I was about to say goodbye, the girl asked if I’d had lunch.
我正要道别时，小女孩问我吃过午饭没有。

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:49.950
After they left, I got into my Jeep and opened the paper bag.
他们走后，我坐进吉普车，打开了那个纸袋。
